WEBVTT

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:06.009
The world subsystem holds what a frame looks at:

00:00:06.109 --> 00:00:10.146
scenes that register objects, cameras that view them, lights

00:00:10.246 --> 00:00:13.110
that shade them, and overlays drawn on top.

00:00:15.033 --> 00:00:19.156
createScene makes a registration container with typed collections

00:00:19.256 --> 00:00:21.885
for meshes and each of the five scientific

00:00:21.985 --> 00:00:24.938
primitives, plus lights and a background color.

00:00:25.366 --> 00:00:27.766
The background color is set when the scene

00:00:27.866 --> 00:00:30.920
is created, or later through its background property.

00:00:31.333 --> 00:00:35.100
add and remove dispatch on the object's type, and typed

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:38.124
helpers clear or find one family at a time.

00:00:38.533 --> 00:00:43.412
Hierarchy is not stored in the scene: parent-child structure lives in

00:00:43.512 --> 00:00:47.670
transforms, so the scene stays a flat set of registrations.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:53.537
traverse and traverseVisible walk the meshes, findByName and findAllByName

00:00:53.637 --> 00:00:57.728
look objects up, and getBounds measures the whole scene.

00:00:58.133 --> 00:01:01.284
clear only removes references, while destroy

00:01:01.384 --> 00:01:04.092
also destroys every registered object.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:10.264
createCamera.perspective takes a vertical field of view in

00:01:10.364 --> 00:01:13.499
degrees, near and far planes, and an aspect

00:01:13.599 --> 00:01:17.036
ratio that can follow the canvas automatically.

00:01:17.466 --> 00:01:21.164
Setting far to infinity gives an infinite far plane.

00:01:21.566 --> 00:01:26.612
createCamera.orthographic uses left, right, top, and bottom bounds

00:01:26.712 --> 00:01:30.277
instead, so size does not change with distance.

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:35.112
Perspective cameras also support a fixed aspect, and glTF

00:01:35.212 --> 00:01:40.178
import preserves authored aspect ratios and infinite far planes.

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:45.077
Both cameras own a transform, so lookAt and setWorldPosition move

00:01:45.177 --> 00:01:49.865
them, and they cache view, projection, and view-projection matrices.

00:01:51.766 --> 00:01:56.208
createLight builds ambient, directional, point, and spot lights, each

00:01:56.308 --> 00:01:59.368
with a color, an intensity, and an enabled flag.

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:02.250
Point and spot lights add a range, and

00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:05.204
spot lights add inner and outer cone angles.

00:02:05.633 --> 00:02:09.960
The renderer packs at most eight non-ambient lights per frame,

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:14.173
and lights imported from glTF follow their node transforms.

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:17.709
Directional lights can also cast shadows through the

00:02:17.809 --> 00:02:20.857
effects facade, which the Render section describes.

00:02:22.766 --> 00:02:26.510
createOverlay.system adds a DOM layer next to the

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:30.432
canvas, where overlay layers are registered by ID.

00:02:30.833 --> 00:02:35.652
It redraws only when something invalidates it, such as the camera, the

00:02:35.752 --> 00:02:40.290
viewport, a layout change, a scale, a colormap, or an interaction.

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:42.872
Binding the controls lets camera

00:02:42.972 --> 00:02:45.997
motion invalidate the overlay automatically.

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:50.460
A layer can be hidden with setLayerEnabled without detaching

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:53.788
it, and removing a layer releases its resources.

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:57.696
The axis triad shows the world axes in a screen corner,

00:02:57.796 --> 00:03:02.078
and the grid draws a labeled reference plane with adaptive spacing.

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:06.308
The legend reads an object's scale transform and colormap, and

00:03:06.408 --> 00:03:09.461
draws a color bar with ticks from that same state.

00:03:11.366 --> 00:03:15.698
To recap: scenes as flat registries, two camera types, four

00:03:15.798 --> 00:03:20.205
light types, and overlays that update only when invalidated.

00:03:21.633 --> 00:03:25.650
The full reference is in the World section of the documentation.
